                <pb facs="0685" n="605" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg605"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Powell to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-06-30"><hi rendition="#italic">June 30,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Powell reports that a telegram received from Cape Haitian states that the
                    admiral fired on the city, killing several people; that Firmin leaves Cape
                    Haitien on Haitian naval vessel under protection of consuls, and that all is
                    quiet at Port au Prince.)</p>
            </div>
